Hi Stephen and Eric,

thank you so much for the quick answers. I tried new models based on your advices - half-normal with a stronger truncation (2.6km) and no alpha transects. The only half-normal model that fitted was the one with no covariates, and the abundance was very small compared to hazard-rate models (N=470). I don't have enough detections to do an estimate per survey, that's why I am using replicates and put survey as a covariate, but it did not fit in this model.

I was very impressed with the difference in estimates between model functions! Should I be more confident with this model?

Indeed we have some issues with data. I believe that the fact that we use a boat of minimum height (4.5m) and the observers looking a lot at the bow contributed to this spike in the detection function (I attached the new one).

Jéssica

